<article class="env-lemma" id="0FL5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FL5">Lemma <span data-tag="0FL5">50.2.1</span>.</a> Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X' \ar[r]_ f \ar[d] &  X \ar[d] \\  S' \ar[r] &  S }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a cartesian diagram of schemes. Then the maps discussed above induce isomorphisms $f^*\Omega ^ p_{X/S} \to \Omega ^ p_{X'/S'}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01V0" data-tag="01V0">29.33.10</a> with the fact that formation of exterior power commutes with base change. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
